<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσυμν-ήτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσιμνάτας</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>judge, umpire</i> at games, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.258
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>overseer, bailiff</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.48
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ruler chosen</i> by the people, <i>elective monarch</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1285a31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1295a14
			</span></i>, Arg.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
			</span></i>; compared with the Roman <i>dictator</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				5.73
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> title of
			magistrates in Greek cities, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.15
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Megara</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				3045
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Chalcedon</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> epith. of Dionysus in Achaia, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				7.21.6
			</span></i> :— fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰσυμνῆτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
